C. Statistical Power Analysis for the ISV

C.1 Clopper–Pearson Confidence Intervals

We desire a margin of error m \leq 0.02 with 95% confidence for the overall fidelity estimate. Using the Clopper–Pearson exact interval for a binomial proportion, with N = 500 and observed fidelity \hat{\phi} \approx 0.95, the 95% confidence interval is approximately (0.928, 0.967), giving margin m = 0.0195. Hence N=500 meets the target for the global fidelity estimate.

C.2 Stratified Sampling Design

The dataset is stratified by regulatory article such that 20 high‑priority articles each receive a minimum of 25 incidents. For articles with low expected incidence, synthetically generated variants (using the LTN rule engine with plausible atom perturbations) augment the stratum to reach n_s = 25. The per‑stratum margin at 95% confidence is \approx 0.15, which is acceptable for regulatory assessment where qualitative expert review supplements quantitative metrics.

