F. Evaluation Datasets and Graph Generator

F.1 SynthChain Dataset Profile

SynthChain is a near‑production testbed providing multi‑source runtime telemetry with chain‑level ground truth across seven supply‑chain exploit scenarios: typosquatting, dependency confusion, malicious maintainer takeover, build‑time injection, container image poisoning, API credential leak, and LLM‑powered agent misuse. Data includes commit logs, API traces, and vendor metadata for 500 simulated applications over 6 months.

F.2 MalwareBench and NPM Benchmark Summary

MalwareBench contains 20,792 packages (npm, PyPI) of which 6,659 are malicious, labelled with behaviour categories (data exfiltration, crypto mining, credential theft, etc.) and 8 evasion techniques. The NPM Malware Benchmark (2026) provides 6,420 malicious and 7,288 benign packages, annotated at the commit level with ground truth.

F.3 G2A2 Generator Configuration

The G2A2 graph generator is configured to match the RASCDS node/edge schema. Parameters: 10,000–100,000 nodes, edge probability 0.005, dynamic rewiring rate 0.01 per epoch. Attack injection: SockPuppet (gradual reputation building over 50 epochs), poisoning, and evasion attack graphs are inserted with labelled ground truth.

